For browser automation, scraping, or UI verification, first read
`/Users/claude/browser-harness/SKILL.md` in full. Codex does not expand
Claude-style `@file` imports in project instructions.

Browser-window hygiene is mandatory. Prefer Codex's in-app Browser when it is
available. Never navigate the operator's Chrome to
`chrome://inspect/#remote-debugging`, open a Chrome profile picker, or bootstrap
or restart `browser-harness` merely because a task needs UI verification. An
agent may use the existing Chrome harness only after a direct attach attempt
shows that it is already available, or when the operator explicitly requests
Chrome. Reuse one existing daemon and tab set, finalize task-owned tabs, and
stop an idle task-named daemon before finishing. The Clip renderer's isolated
headless Chrome is not a substitute for user-browser automation.

## ProxyWar

ProxyWar is an OpenFrontIO fork/product layer where developers and AI hobbyists connect autonomous agents, run OpenFront matches, watch rendered replays, and inspect decision artifacts.

Internal agent infrastructure is still called AI Nations League.

Current scope lock (2026-06-13): Proxy War is going all in on Softmax. Active
work is limited to Coworld integration and the competitive agent. The older
trusted-private-beta, external-agent onboarding, `/public`, and `/agent-start`
work remains historical context and maintenance-only unless the operator
explicitly reactivates it.

Operating lead (2026-07-13): Codex is the single user-facing Control lead for
this workspace. Codex owns prioritization, bounded delegation, integration,
verification, and durable project-state updates. Claude-era operational files
remain historical reference; `.codex/` is the active local operating layer.

Current local workspace path: `/Users/claude/Documents/proxywar_main`.

Repository model: `https://github.com/0xNad/ProxyWar` is the platform/protocol source of truth. The public `https://github.com/0xNad/ProxyWar-starter-agent` repo is the external-agent template and should be synced from `examples/external-agent/`; it must not define a separate protocol, validator, runner, or raw-intent path.

Start broad project work by reading:

- `docs/project-state/context-for-new-codex-threads.md`
- `docs/project-state/2026-06-13-coworld-agent-scope-lock.md`
- `docs/project-state/KEYSTONE.md`
